      "writtenOn": "2024-11-23T21:43:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh you\u0027re right that is confusing. LEVEL_NO_PENDING is actually not an error but rather a status.\n\nThe normal flow would be:\n- a successful trySetHdcpLevel\n- getPendingHdcpLevel returning STATUS_LEVEL_NO_PENDING\n- getHdcpLevel\n- verify that currentLevel \u003e\u003d previous trySetHdcpLevel request\n\nThe error case would be:\ncurrentLevel \u003c previous trySetHdcpLevel request\n\ndo you agree?\n\nI have updated the interface as to not conflate error and state. PTAL!",
      "parentUuid": "f7c8aebf_1342de79",
